{"hasPermission(ClientModel, String) looks up client resources using resourceServer.getId() as the owner filter, but client resources are created with resourceServer.getClientId() as the owner, so per-client permissions are silently ignored and only global 'all clients' permissions take effect": 0.5801913142204285, "getClientsWithPermission iterates resources by type 'Clients', but client-instance resources created via AdminPermissionsSchema.getOrCreateResource are stored with no explicit type (defaults to null), causing the method to miss all per-client resources and return an incomplete set": 0.6903799772262573, "canManage(ClientModel client) only checks the legacy MANAGE_CLIENTS role or a resource-specific permission for that client, but does not check the realm-wide fine-grained manage permission on the Clients resource type, causing admins with only the global V2 manage permission to be incorrectly denied": 0.5687388777732849, "canView() returns false for admins who have only the all-clients manage permission, breaking realm-wide client visibility since the manage scope should subsume view but the implementation only checks canViewClientDefault() and the view scope": 0.7848647832870483, "When getOrCreateResource creates a client resource, it sets name to client.getId() but never calls setDisplayName, and getResourceName only special-cases Users, causing client permission listings to show null instead of a human-readable name": 0.7556491494178772, "hasGrantedPermission() only evaluates the passed resource, so getClientsWithPermission() misses permissions granted through the shared 'all clients' resource, returning an empty set even when canView(client)/canManage(client) would succeed for those clients": 0.7466685771942139}